    "My friend invite me to a party last night but I didn't know it was formal event, a crucial piece of information that was apparently lost in translation or simply never conveyed to me, leading to an utterly embarrassing and uncomfortable situation, as I shows up wearing casual clothes, a simple t-shirt and jeans, while everyone else was elegantly dressing fancy, adorned in glittering gowns and sharp suits, making me feel incredibly out of place and foolish, immediately wanting to leave and disappear into the night, but she insist me to stayed, pulling me further into the crowded room, reassuring me it was fine, though I felt anything but, and the music was too loud, a thumping bass that vibrated through my chest and made coherent conversation almost impossible, and peoples was shouting instead of talking, straining their voices to be heard over the deafening volume, creating a chaotic and unpleasant atmosphere, also, the food wasn't taste good, a collection of bland and uninspired dishes that hardly justified the formal setting, and there were no enough drinks, leaving many guests, including myself, parched and dissatisfied, further adding to the general sense of disappointment, then, to make matters worse, one guy accidentally poured juice on my shoes, a clumsy mishap that added insult to injury, and just says sorry like it nothing happen, offering a perfunctory apology without any genuine concern or offer to help clean up the sticky mess, confirming my growing conviction that this entire evening was a mistake, and I think I shouldn't have come there in first place, a thought that replayed endlessly in my mind, it was the worsted party I ever been, a truly miserable experience from start to finish, and I sincerely hope I not going to another soon, wishing for quieter, more comfortable gatherings in the future where I can actually hear myself think and wear whatever I please without feeling like a social pariah, having endured enough social discomfort for a lifetime.",
